From 38b04a4a255cecb318b6dc4325b79589c94ee1ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:04:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): upstream-sync diagnostics: owner match works with
 real kanban show, incomplete logs stay unknown [daveey]

Exact-head review of ad6bc7467e1 found:
- kanban show --json has no idempotency_key, so owner matching never succeeded live.
  Provenance is now state key->id + created_by nightly-e2e + open + the body listing
  exactly the set (a key, when a board returns one, must still match).
- An unparsed/unavailable candidate e2e log printed 'no open card matches'; now 'owner
  lookup unknown'. A corrupt state file raises into 'lookup unavailable'.
- Whole-file crash/collection/no-tests/timeout sections mark a log's id set incomplete,
  so main-side crashes can no longer yield 'candidate-only'.
- Oldest nightlies after the base are read first; log reads share a 300 s budget.
